      <div class="split">
        <div class="body-copy fade" style="--d:.1s">
          <p>
            It started in Grade 5 with Scratch. I thought I was making games and animations.
            Nobody told me it was code. By Grade 9 it was Java in Greenfoot, and robotics was
            a compulsory subject I would have taken anyway.
          </p>
          <p>
            My dad was already deep in robotics, so it became ours. We woke up at 5am most
            mornings to work through robotics projects and maths before school. Grade 10
            brought Information Technology, and that was the end of the debate about what I
            was going to do with my life.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-bottom:0">
            Now I am in my final year in Cape Town, co-leading a technology education
            initiative and heading a five-person team building software for a community
            organisation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <ul class="facts fade" style="--d:.2s">
          <li><b>Known as</b><span>Kwethu</span></li>
          <li><b>Based</b><span>Rondebosch, Cape Town</span></li>
          <li><b>From</b><span>Durban, KwaZulu-Natal</span></li>
          <li><b>Studying</b><span>BCIS in Application Development</span></li>
          <li><b>At</b><span>EMERIS (The IIE), Cape Town &middot; 2024 to 2026</span></li>
          <li><b>School</b><span>Crawford International La Lucia, Durban</span></li>
          <li><b>Writes</b><span>Java, C#, Kotlin, Python, SQL, JavaScript</span></li>
          <li><b>Builds with</b><span>Android Studio, ASP.NET Core, Firebase, Azure, Docker</span></li>
        </ul>
