      <div class="projects">

        <article class="project">
          <figure class="project-art wipe" style="margin:0">
            <img src="/images/philisa-team.webp" alt="The Philisa Abafazi Bethu project team">
          </figure>
          <div class="fade" style="--d:.15s">
            <span class="project-n">Project 01 &middot; Non-profit organisation</span>
            <h3>Philisa Abafazi Bethu</h3>
            <p class="role">Project lead &middot; Five-person team &middot; 2026</p>
            <p class="body-copy">
              Philisa Abafazi Bethu, meaning &ldquo;Heal Our Women&rdquo; in isiXhosa, is a
              non-profit organisation in Lavender Hill, Cape Town, supporting women and children.
              We met with their team to understand how they actually work, then built two
              products for them: an Android app where volunteers manage tasks, join programmes
              and reach coordinators, and a web platform opening up their support services and
              resources to the community. I gathered the requirements from their staff,
              translated their operational problems into system requirements, and ran the
              sprints, task allocation and code review across the team. We set up an expo to
              present the work back to them.
            </p>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li>Kotlin</li><li>Firebase</li><li>Android Studio</li><li>Azure</li><li>Docker</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <figure class="project-art wipe" style="margin:0">
            <img src="/images/bystudents-demo.png" alt="The By Students app presented on a laptop">
          </figure>
          <div class="fade" style="--d:.15s">
            <span class="project-n">Project 02 &middot; University</span>
            <h3>By Students</h3>
            <p class="role">Project lead &amp; developer &middot; 2026</p>
            <p class="body-copy">
              A marketplace connecting students to student-owned businesses and services. My
              group and I designed the application architecture and REST API, wired Firebase
              Authentication into the database layer, and built distance-based discovery with
              business profiles and categorised messaging for enquiries, bookings and quotes.
              We added biometric sign-in and offline browsing so the app still holds up on a
              bad connection, along with the documentation, testing and GitHub workflow
              behind it.
            </p>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li>Kotlin</li><li>Firebase Auth</li><li>REST API</li><li>Biometrics</li><li>Offline</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <figure class="project-art wipe" style="margin:0">
            <img src="/images/frc-team.webp" alt="Working on the Team 10399 robot at the competition">
          </figure>
          <div class="fade" style="--d:.15s">
            <span class="project-n">Project 03 &middot; Independent</span>
            <h3>Team 10399</h3>
            <p class="role">Designer &amp; developer &middot; Ongoing</p>
            <p class="body-copy">
              The platform for Team 10399, the FIRST Robotics team I help run through Rooted
              Tech. Team information, outreach and competition updates in one place, deployed
              on Azure and built to grow with the team instead of being rebuilt every season.
              Built because the team needed it, not for a mark.
            </p>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li>ASP.NET Core MVC</li><li>Azure</li><li>C#</li><li>Branding</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

